nemia hemolítica may also be associated with certain types of glucogenosis, which are metabolic disorders affecting glycogen storage and utilization.", "CONVULSIONES:Convulsiones are seizures that can occur in patients with certain types of glucogenosis, particularly those affecting the nervous system. Additionally, convulsiones can also manifest in severe cases of hyponatremia.", "BIOPSIA DE TEJIDO HEPÁTICO:Biopsia de tejido hepático is a diagnostic procedure used to assess liver conditions, including glucogenosis.)<|COMPLETE|>", "CARDIOMIOPATÍA:Cardiomiopatía is a condition characterized by heart muscle disease, which can lead to heart failure and other complications.", "LAFLORA:Lafora is associated with a genetic condition known as Lafora disease, which involves a deficiency of laforin and leads to various neurological symptoms.", "GLUCOGENOSIS TIPO I:Glucogenosis tipo I is a metabolic disorder affecting the body's ability to break down glycogen, leading to various health complications.", "GLYCOSADE:Glycosade is a modified starch that helps maintain blood glucose levels during fasting periods, particularly useful for patients with metabolic disorders.", "VON GIERKE TYPE IA:Von Gierke Type Ia is a specific type of hepatic glycogen storage disease characterized by a deficiency in glucose-6-phosphatase, leading to severe hypoglycemia and other metabolic complications.", "GM-CSF:Granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor (GM-CSF) is a cytokine used in the treatment of certain metabolic disorders to stimulate the production of white blood cells.", "G-CSF:Granulocyte colony-stimulating factor (G-CSF) is a cytokine that promotes the production of neutrophils and is used in the treatment of neutropenia in metabolic disorders.", "CALCIO Y VITAMINA D:Calcium and vitamin D are essential nutrients that may be beneficial as supplements in the treatment of hepatic glycogen storage diseases.", "IECA:IECA, or angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors, are medications recommended for patients experiencing microalbuminuria, particularly in the context of metabolic disorders. These medications play a crucial role in managing conditions associated with kidney function and protein excretion. Additionally, it has been noted that IECA may be associated with the occurrence of diarrhea as a side effect.", "PHENYLALANINE HYDROXYLASE DEFICIENCY:Phenylalanine hydroxylase deficiency is a metabolic disorder that affects the body's ability to process phenylalanine, leading to various health issues if untreated.", "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF HUMAN GENETICS:The European Journal of Human Genetics publishes research related to human genetics, including studies on phenylketonuria."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}